{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.CategoricalTransferMatrix","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.CategoricalTransferMatrix","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.FiberBundle.Basic"],"declarations":31,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.transfer_matrix_level_independence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.transfer_matrix_level_independence","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-transfer-matrix.lean#L175-L187","doc":"**Level independence, in the form that is true.**\n\nTwo transfer matrices with the same bi-filtration have the same derived\nvolume.  Note the hypothesis is on the **filtration**, not on `base`: the\nbraiding data is what the volume depends on, and equal bases say nothing.\nThat substitution is the whole content of the correction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.DerivedVertexVolume.volume_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.DerivedVertexVolume.volume_eq","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-transfer-matrix.lean#L173-L173","doc":"The volume is determined by the reduction — the `.md`'s\n\"depends only on the Markov trace of the Hecke-reduced element\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.DerivedVertexVolume.volume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.DerivedVertexVolume.volume","kind":"def","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-transfer-matrix.lean#L170-L170","doc":"The vertex volume of a transfer matrix. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.DerivedVertexVolume.reduce","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.DerivedVertexVolume.reduce","kind":"def","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-transfer-matrix.lean#L168-L168","doc":"The Hecke-reduced invariant of a bi-filtration. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.DerivedVertexVolume.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.DerivedVertexVolume.mk","kind":"ctor","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-transfer-matrix.lean#L166-L166","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.DerivedVertexVolume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.DerivedVertexVolume","kind":"structure","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-transfer-matrix.lean#L160-L173","doc":"**Vertex volume DERIVED from the Hecke reduction**, which is what the\n`.md` actually describes.\n\n`reduce` is the Markov trace of the Hecke-reduced element (abstracted\nhere as a function of the bi-filtration); `volume_eq` says a transfer\nmatrix's volume *is* that reduction rather than independent data. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.level_independence_false_as_stated","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.level_independence_false_as_stated","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-transfer-matrix.lean#L151-L158","doc":"**The former axiom is false.**  Same base, different volume: nothing in\n`CategoricalTransferMatrix` ties the two together. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.trivialFiltration","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.trivialFiltration","kind":"def","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-transfer-matrix.lean#L142-L149","doc":"The empty bi-filtration, used only to witness the refutation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.trivialConfig","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.trivialConfig","kind":"def","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-transfer-matrix.lean#L136-L140","doc":"The empty insertion configuration, used only to witness the refutation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.InteractionBiFiltration.step_preserves_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.InteractionBiFiltration.step_preserves_bound","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-transfer-matrix.lean#L105-L110","doc":"Adding a crossing while advancing the jet level preserves the\nbi-filtration invariant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalTransferMatrix.vertex_volume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalTransferMatrix.vertex_volume","kind":"def","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-transfer-matrix.lean#L103-L103","doc":"The vertex volume polynomial (the invariant). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalTransferMatrix.filtration","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalTransferMatrix.filtration","kind":"def","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-transfer-matrix.lean#L101-L101","doc":"The bi-filtration: jet level (ascending) and accumulated\nHecke relations (descending) at the current Planck step. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalTransferMatrix.base","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalTransferMatrix.base","kind":"def","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-transfer-matrix.lean#L98-L98","doc":"The exceptional divisor where braiding takes place, carried as a\n**type parameter** `B` rather than by naming `ExceptionalDivisor`.\n\nTwo reasons, and the second is the load-bearing one. `ExceptionalDivisor`\nis declared in a *sibling* (`quantum-observable-universes/exceptional-divisor.lean`)\nwhich this file cannot import — siblings sit outside the Lake globs — and\nin the library as `structure ExceptionalDivisor (M : Type*)` in\n`QOU/ArchimedeanUniverse.lean`, i.e. on the **archimedean** side of the\n§7c wall, while this file is over the categorical `R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]`.\nNaming either here would straddle the wall.\n\nWith `autoImplicit` on, the bare name became an auto-bound variable and\nthe errors surfaced three levels downstream, as\n`don't know how to synthesize implicit argument α` on `T₁.base = T₂.base`.\n`set_option autoImplicit false` above makes that a name error instead. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalTransferMatrix.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalTransferMatrix.mk","kind":"ctor","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-transfer-matrix.lean#L82-L82","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalTransferMatrix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalTransferMatrix","kind":"structure","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-transfer-matrix.lean#L77-L103","doc":"The categorical transfer matrix: equivalence class of braiding\noperations on a hadron that produce the same vertex volume. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:categorical-transfer-matrix","label":"def:categorical-transfer-matrix","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-transfer-matrix.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.InteractionBiFiltration.crossing_distinct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.InteractionBiFiltration.crossing_distinct","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-transfer-matrix.lean#L75-L75","doc":"Each crossing is between distinct slots. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.InteractionBiFiltration.crossingPairs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.InteractionBiFiltration.crossingPairs","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-transfer-matrix.lean#L73-L73","doc":"The ordered sequence of crossing pairs (slot i, slot j). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.InteractionBiFiltration.crossings_le_jet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.InteractionBiFiltration.crossings_le_jet","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-transfer-matrix.lean#L71-L71","doc":"Crossing number cannot exceed jet level:\na knot with c crossings requires at least c Planck steps. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.InteractionBiFiltration.numCrossings","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.InteractionBiFiltration.numCrossings","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-transfer-matrix.lean#L68-L68","doc":"Total number of crossings resolved so far. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.InteractionBiFiltration.jetLevel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.InteractionBiFiltration.jetLevel","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-transfer-matrix.lean#L66-L66","doc":"Current jet level (Planck step count). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.InteractionBiFiltration.config","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.InteractionBiFiltration.config","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-transfer-matrix.lean#L64-L64","doc":"The underlying insertion configuration. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.InteractionBiFiltration.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.InteractionBiFiltration.mk","kind":"ctor","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-transfer-matrix.lean#L62-L62","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.InteractionBiFiltration","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.InteractionBiFiltration","kind":"structure","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-transfer-matrix.lean#L49-L75","doc":"The interaction bi-filtration on the configuration space algebra.\n\nTwo filtrations act simultaneously:\n\n1. **Ascending (jet prolongation).**  The brane tower\nA_0 ↪ A_1 ↪ A_2 ↪ ⋯ grows with each Planck step.\n\n2. **Descending (Hecke relations).**  Within a given jet level,\neach crossing adds a relation to the interaction ideal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.InsertionConfig.distinct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.InsertionConfig.distinct","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-transfer-matrix.lean#L47-L47","doc":"Distinct insertion points: z_i ≠ z_j for i ≠ j.\nThis is the configuration space constraint; collisions\nproduce OPE singularities (z_i − z_j)^{−k}. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.InsertionConfig.points","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.InsertionConfig.points","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-transfer-matrix.lean#L43-L43","doc":"The insertion points z_1, …, z_n as affine coordinates on 𝒮_p. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.InsertionConfig.n","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.InsertionConfig.n","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-transfer-matrix.lean#L41-L41","doc":"Number of constituent slots. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.InsertionConfig.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.InsertionConfig.mk","kind":"ctor","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-transfer-matrix.lean#L39-L39","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.InsertionConfig","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.InsertionConfig","kind":"structure","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-transfer-matrix.lean#L35-L47","doc":"The ordered configuration space Conf_n(𝒮_p): n-tuples of distinct\ninsertion points on the exceptional divisor.  The index i labels\nthe constituent slot (not the knot type), so multiple slots may\ncarry the same simple object. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.q_inv_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.q_inv_param","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-transfer-matrix.lean#L33-L33","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.q_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.q_param","kind":"def","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-transfer-matrix.lean#L32-L32","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.R_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.R_q","kind":"def","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/categorical-transfer-matrix.lean#L29-L31","doc":"Ground ring `R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` (Laurent polynomials over ℤ).\nSee `QOU.Archimedean.GroundRing` for the compiled definition. ","signatureChunk":0}]}